<title>USA: Group holds 9.6 pct of Pacific Sunwear.</title>
<headline>Group holds 9.6 pct of Pacific Sunwear.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group that includes Boston investment manager Jeffrey Vinik, his associates and business entities, said Tuesday it has acquired 770,000 shares of Pacific Sunwear of California Inc., or 9.6 percent of the total.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it acquired the stake for $20.2 million for investment purposes.</p>
<p>It said it acquired the stake between Nov. 1 and 25 at prices ranging from $23.25 to $27.797 a share.</p>
</text>
